@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #000000
skinparam ComponentFontColor #000000
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #000000
skinparam RectangleFontColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseFontColor #000000

title Product Operating Model After PM Toolkit Expansion

actor "LLM / Agent" as Agent #E8F0FE
component "Product Management Engine" as Engine #D0E0FF
component "Backlog Analyzer\nstale + cycle ranking" as Analyzer #D9EAD3
component "Governance Gap Auditor\nmetrics + guardrails + kill criteria" as Auditor #FFF4CC
component "Initiative Scorecard\nRICE / ICE / WSJF / opportunity" as Scorecard #EADCF8
component "Outcome Roadmap Builder\nNow / Next / Later / Park" as Roadmap #D9EAD3
component "Portfolio Review\ncore / adjacent / transformational" as Portfolio #FCE5CD
component "Signal Vetting Gate\nevidence quality + decision reversal" as Vetting #FFE5E5
component "Issue Creation\nLinear / GitHub opportunity templates" as Creator #FCE5CD
database "Linear + GitHub Work" as Work #EAF7EA

Agent --> Engine : analyze backlog
Engine --> Analyzer : score live work
Analyzer --> Work : read issues and cycles
Analyzer --> Auditor : inspect descriptions for PM governance gaps
Analyzer --> Roadmap : derive planning slices
Analyzer --> Portfolio : classify current work mix
Engine --> Agent : stale report,\nroadmap,\nportfolio,\ngovernance gaps

Agent --> Engine : score initiatives
Engine --> Scorecard : apply selected framework
Scorecard --> Auditor : reject weakly governed bets
Scorecard --> Roadmap : build Now / Next / Later / Park
Scorecard --> Portfolio : compare against target mix
Engine --> Agent : ranked roadmap plan

Agent --> Engine : create proactive issues
Engine --> Vetting : require evidence quality,\noutcome metric,\nguardrails,\nkill criteria,\nprivacy/security/accessibility
Vetting --> Creator : qualified signal only
Creator --> Work : create governed issue

note bottom of Engine #F3F3F3
The MCP server now acts as an operating system
for product decisions: it scores bets consistently,
forces measurable outcomes and guardrails,
preserves kill criteria, and keeps roadmap work
balanced against portfolio strategy.
end note

@enduml
